transfer.md\",\"text\":\"transfer\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"learning_003\",\"category\":\"learning\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"A learned procedure contains an intentional mistake that can silently produce a plausible but wrong result. Detect it using independent validation, correct the reusable procedure rather than only the output, rerun the workflow, and record the corrected rule and evidence without erasing the correction history.\",\"mode\":\"warm\",\"tags\":[\"learning\",\"correction\",\"silent_failure\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"skills/reporting_workflow.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/learning_correction.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/learning_correction.md\",\"text\":\"Correction\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"long_horizon_001\",\"category\":\"long_horizon\",\"tier\":4,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Complete an end-to-end workflow: inspect the workspace, identify authoritative data, plan, build analysis, execute it, recover from an error, generate the deliverable, validate every requirement, and write a changelog. Keep the process compatible with a 98k context; use compaction or durable notes instead of restarting from scratch.\",\"tags\":[\"long_horizon\",\"recovery\",\"98k_context\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/long_horizon_changelog.md\",\"weight\":1,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/long_horizon_changelog.md\",\"text\":\"Validation\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"min_lines\",\"path\":\"reports/long_horizon_changelog.md\",\"lines\":8,\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"long_horizon_002\",\"category\":\"long_horizon\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Implement the requested reporting feature across multiple files, run existing checks, diagnose and fix regressions, update documentation, test invalid inputs, and leave the workspace verified. Maintain a dependency chain between changes and checks. Use compaction or durable notes when useful within the 98k context.\",\"tags\":[\"long_horizon\",\"coding\",\"98k_context\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"command\",\"command\":\"python -m pytest -q\",\"timeout\":60,\"weight\":4,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"README.md\",\"weight\":1,\"fatal\":true}]},\n{\"id\":\"long_horizon_003\",\"category\":\"long_horizon\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Investigate the supplied business problem, gather evidence from multiple workspace sources, reconcile contradictions, create a supporting tool if useful, produce the final deliverable, then audit every original requirement and correct omissions. Maintain durable notes so the workflow can survive context compaction.\",\"tags\":[\"long_horizon\",\"audit\",\"tools\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/final_audit.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/final_audit.md\",\"text\":\"Requirement\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/final_audit.md\",\"text\":\"Evidence\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"memory_001\",\"category\":\"memory\",\"tier\":3,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Learn these durable workflow preferences: Python for small automation tools, simple maintainable tools, and never create a Git commit without explicit approval. Distinguish durable preferences from temporary instructions, store only durable preferences, and confirm what you retained.\",\"mode\":\"cold\",\"tags\":[\"memory\",\"scope\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_note.md\",\"text\":\"Python\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_note.md\",\"text\":\"commit\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"memory_002\",\"category\":\"memory\",\"tier\":4,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Create a small automation tool while respecting previously stored workflow preferences. Retrieve memory rather than asking the user to repeat it, demonstrate that at least two preferences affected implementation, and do not create a Git commit.\",\"mode\":\"warm\",\"tags\":[\"memory\",\"application\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_application.md\",\"weight\":1,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_application.md\",\"text\":\"preference\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"memory_003\",\"category\":\"memory\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"The durable preference for new automation tools has changed from Python to TypeScript. Update retained knowledge without deleting unrelated preferences, explain conflict resolution, create the new tool using TypeScript, and verify the old Python preference is no longer applied to new tools while the no-commit rule remains.\",\"mode\":\"warm\",\"tags\":[\"memory\",\"update\",\"conflict_resolution\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_update.md\",\"weight\":1,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_update.md\",\"text\":\"TypeScript\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_update.md\",\"text\":\"no-commit\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"memory_004\",\"category\":\"memory\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Create another small automation tool using the current durable preferences. Retrieve memory, preserve the distinction between new TypeScript tools and existing Python tools, verify the project structure, and explicitly check that no forbidden Git commit was created. Save reports/memory_consistency.md.\",\"mode\":\"warm\",\"tags\":[\"memory\",\"consistency\",\"negative_constraint\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_consistency.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_consistency.md\",\"text\":\"TypeScript\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/memory_consistency.md\",\"text\":\"commit\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"subagents_001\",\"category\":\"subagents\",\"tier\":4,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Analyze the supplied documents and produce a comparative report. Decompose into independent research streams when useful, delegate only when it improves correctness or efficiency, then reconcile duplicate and conflicting claims yourself.\",\"tags\":[\"delegation\",\"reconciliation\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_comparison.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_comparison.md\",\"text\":\"Source\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_comparison.md\",\"text\":\"Conflict\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"subagents_002\",\"category\":\"subagents\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Solve a multi-part research and implementation task. Decide which subtasks to delegate, give precise scopes and acceptance criteria, critically review delegated outputs, resolve conflicts, and integrate only verified findings into one final deliverable.\",\"tags\":[\"delegation\",\"synthesis\",\"verification\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_synthesis.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_synthesis.md\",\"text\":\"Verified\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_synthesis.md\",\"text\":\"Rejected\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"subagents_003\",\"category\":\"subagents\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Coordinate a small project using subagents where appropriate: one stream inspects evidence and another inspects implementation constraints. Reconcile their outputs, reject unsupported conclusions, and produce one decision memo with traceable evidence and a verification checklist.\",\"tags\":[\"delegation\",\"architecture\",\"audit\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_decision.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_decision.md\",\"text\":\"Verification\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/subagent_decision.md\",\"text\":\"Evidence\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"tool_use_001\",\"category\":\"tool_use\",\"tier\":3,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Inspect the workspace recursively and classify files as authoritative, historical/secondary, or decoys based on contents rather than filenames. Report the classification without modifying anything and save reports/file_classification.md.\",\"tags\":[\"filesystem\",\"read_only\",\"classification\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/file_classification.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/file_classification.md\",\"text\":\"Authoritative\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/file_classification.md\",\"text\":\"Decoy\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"tool_use_002\",\"category\":\"tool_use\",\"tier\":4,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Read README.md, follow its references to configuration and implementation files, resolve indirection, and report the effective settings. Verify them against consumer code or tests. Do not edit files. Save reports/effective_config.md.\",\"tags\":[\"filesystem\",\"navigation\",\"verification\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"exists\",\"path\":\"reports/effective_config.md\",\"weight\":2,\"fatal\":true},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/effective_config.md\",\"text\":\"effective\",\"weight\":1},{\"type\":\"contains\",\"path\":\"reports/effective_config.md\",\"text\":\"verified\",\"weight\":1}]},\n{\"id\":\"tool_use_003\",\"category\":\"tool_use\",\"tier\":5,\"revision\":2,\"prompt\":\"Run the provided test command, diagnose the failure, identify the single file responsible, fix only that file, rerun the complete suite, and prove the original failure is gone. Do not weaken tests or alter expectations.\",\"tags\":[\"execution\",\"recovery\",\"minimal_change\"],\"acceptance\":[{\"type\":\"command\",\"command\":\"python -m pytest -q\",\"timeout\":45,\"weight\":4,\"fatal\":true}]}\n]\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":